    /// <summary>
    /// Gives itemtemplate_weapon.tool_type real values.
    ///
    /// Every one of the 2440 rows carried 15, which is not a value the client's tooltype table
    /// has - it stops at 12. The client reads the column in two places and both misbehave on it.
    /// The tooltip treats 1-6 as "this is a tool", suppresses the damage line and prints what the
    /// tool does instead; with 15 every tool showed a damage line, and _AddWeaponToolInfo passed
    /// its "greater than zero" guard, matched no branch and inserted a blank line - on every
    /// weapon in the game, not just tools. And weaponreload.py hands the value to reload-modifier
    /// effects that return 0 for a type they do not list, so anything speeding up reload for one
    /// weapon family silently did nothing.
    ///
    /// Unlike the heat placeholders these values are reconstructed rather than chosen. Tools come
    /// from the entity class's attack action id, which is the field the client itself dispatches
    /// on, with TOOL_HARVEST splitting on its arg id - 168 Salvage, 169 Tissue Extraction. The
    /// six gun families the enum names come from the class-name family, cross-checked against the
    /// required skill, which partitions them exactly and disagrees on no row.
    ///
    /// 1428 rows get a value. The other 1012 are left for the last statement to set to 0, which
    /// is the honest answer: they are the eight weapon families the enum has no entry for.
    ///
    /// Up only touches rows still holding 15, so a row corrected by hand is left alone. Down
    /// restores 15 on rows still holding exactly what Up set. The 0 group is the exception - it
    /// cannot be told apart from a hand-set 0 by value, and before this migration no row was 0
    /// at all, so Down takes every remaining 0 back to 15.
    ///
    /// Data only - no schema changes.
    /// </summary>
